  "notes": "{降|ふ}り{出|だ}す is a compound verb ({降|ふ}る + {出|だ}す) meaning to start falling (rain/snow).\n\nCOMPOUND VERB PATTERN:\n〜{出|だ}す indicates the beginning of an action.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {雨|あめ}が{降|ふ}り{出|だ}す (rain starts falling)\n- {雪|ゆき}が{降|ふ}り{出|だ}す (snow starts falling)\n- {急|きゅう}に{降|ふ}り{出|だ}す (suddenly starts raining)\n\nRELATED VERBS:\n- {降|ふ}り{止|や}む: to stop raining/snowing\n- {降|ふ}り{続|つづ}く: to keep raining/snowing",
